-- What works today for numbers, read from the code: the plain stats the calculator reads, each as the quantity it
-- changes and how (from the stat's own name: maximum_life flat for base_maximum_life, increased for maximum_life_+%,
-- more for a _+%_final), and every conditional stat StatConditions.cs decides and counts onto a plain one, with the
-- conditions it asks and the plain stat (counts_as). Written by running StatConditions over all 23,362 stats on main
-- 439072a06. The rows record what the code does; nothing reads them yet, and checked stays 0 until a row is compared.
-- fx_stats: the stats above become handled 'modifier'; a conditional stat whose condition is not modelled, or that
-- nothing reads once its condition is decided, gets its why and fit.
